        "status": true,
        "title": "Peer Review of Carbon Credit Methodology for Jute-Based Net CO2 Emission Reduction",
        "created": "2026-09-08T10:34:19+00:00",
        "changed": "2026-09-08T10:35:59+00:00",
        "promote": false,
        "sticky": false,
        "default_langcode": true,
        "revision_translation_affected": true,
        "metatag": null,
        "path": {
          "alias": "/project/peer-review-carbon-credit-methodology-jute-based-net-co2-emission-reduction",
          "pid": 12693,
          "langcode": "en"
        },
        "body": {
          "value": "<p>TERI is undertaking an independent technical peer review of the “Methodology for Carbon Crediting in Jute Cultivation Systems” (MC-JCS: TJF0001, Version 1.1) developed for The Jute Foundation. The assignment assesses whether the proposed methodology provides a scientifically robust, transparent and practically applicable framework for quantifying greenhouse gas emission reductions and carbon removals associated with jute cultivation systems.</p><p>The review covers the methodology’s scope and applicability, project boundaries, baseline and additionality provisions, treatment of annual jute biomass and soil organic carbon, cultivation- and retting-related emissions, permanence, uncertainty, monitoring, digital traceability and safeguards against double counting. It also examines the supporting calculation coefficients, equations, emission factors and assumptions used to estimate net carbon benefits.</p><p>The project aims to identify technical and methodological gaps and provide recommendations for strengthening the methodology before pilot application or consideration under a carbon-crediting programme. The review will support the development of a more credible and verifiable framework for linking improved jute cultivation practices, sustainable agriculture and farmer livelihoods with carbon-finance opportunities.</p>",
          "format": "full_html",
          "processed": "<p>TERI is undertaking an independent technical peer review of the “Methodology for Carbon Crediting in Jute Cultivation Systems” (MC-JCS: TJF0001, Version 1.1) developed for The Jute Foundation. The assignment assesses whether the proposed methodology provides a scientifically robust, transparent and practically applicable framework for quantifying greenhouse gas emission reductions and carbon removals associated with jute cultivation systems.</p><p>The review covers the methodology’s scope and applicability, project boundaries, baseline and additionality provisions, treatment of annual jute biomass and soil organic carbon, cultivation- and retting-related emissions, permanence, uncertainty, monitoring, digital traceability and safeguards against double counting. It also examines the supporting calculation coefficients, equations, emission factors and assumptions used to estimate net carbon benefits.</p><p>The project aims to identify technical and methodological gaps and provide recommendations for strengthening the methodology before pilot application or consideration under a carbon-crediting programme. The review will support the development of a more credible and verifiable framework for linking improved jute cultivation practices, sustainable agriculture and farmer livelihoods with carbon-finance opportunities.</p>",
          "summary": ""
        },
